{"success": true, "data": {"stdout": "{"doc_id": "Henrik Angell", "input_text": "Henrik August Angell ( 22 August 1861 – 26 January 1922 ) was a Norwegian military officer , sportsman , and writer . He was a ski pioneer and the first Norwegian delegate to the International Olympic Committee . Henrik Angell was born at Luster in Sogn og Fjordane and grew up in Bergen , Norway . He was the son of Johan Mølmann Anderson Lysholm Angell ( 1820 – 88 ) and his wife Marie With Bonnevie ( 1830 – 1904 ) . He received an education at the Norwegian Military Academy and entered the Norwegian Army . He was a Colonel and Regiment Chief from 1911 . He was commander leader of the Søndermør Infantry Regiment until 1914 and of the Smaalenene Infantry Regiment until 1918 . He joined the French Foreign Legion in 1918 , and participated on the Western Front for France in World War I. Angell was admitted to the skiing club SK Ull in 1898 and was a sports advocate . He wrote several books promoting skiing and Norwegian nationalism . He also wrote a series of military history books . He died during 1922 in Kristiania ( now Oslo ) , Norway . His statue by Gustav Lærum is located at Holmenkollen in Oslo .", "gold_entities": [{"text": "Henrik August Angell", "type": "PER"}, {"text": "22 August 1861", "type": "TIME"}, {"text": "26 January 1922", "type": "TIME"}, {"text": "Norwegian", "type": "LOC"}, {"text": "International Olympic Committee", "type": "ORG"}, {"text": "Luster", "type": "LOC"}, {"text": "Sogn og Fjordane", "type": "LOC"}, {"text": "Bergen", "type": "LOC"}, {"text": "Norway", "type": "LOC"}, {"text": "Johan Mølmann Anderson Lysholm Angell", "type": "PER"}, {"text": "1820", "type": "TIME"}, {"text": "88", "type": "TIME"}, {"text": "Marie With Bonnevie", "type": "PER"}, {"text": "1830", "type": "TIME"}, {"text": "1904", "type": "TIME"}, {"text": "Norwegian Military Academy", "type": "ORG"}, {"text": "Norwegian Army", "type": "ORG"}, {"text": "1911", "type": "TIME"}, {"text": "Sønder